   "text": {
    "L1": "Biodiversity means the variety of living things in a place.",
    "L2": "Plants and animals depend on one another, so losing one species can affect many others.",
    "L3": "Here is a worked example: bees carry pollen between mustard flowers.",
    "L4": "If bees become fewer, fewer flowers are pollinated, so fewer pods and seeds form.",
    "L5": "That means less mustard oil and less income for farmers.",
    "L6": "Vultures also have a role: they eat dead animals and clean the surroundings.",
    "L7": "When vultures declined, carcasses rotted longer, stray dogs increased and disease risk rose.",
    "L8": "We conserve diversity by protecting habitats, avoiding pollution and harmful chemicals, and planting native species."
   },
